/*
  DataTableResizer.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0212 · DataTableResizer (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web `components/ui/DataTableResizer.tsx` is an
  anonymous presentational primitive — it builds its accessible label inline (`label ?? \`Resize column
  ${columnKey}\``) and exposes the width numerically through `aria-valuenow`, calling no `t()` of its own —
  so there are NO web keys to mirror here. The entries below are the native VoiceOver additions: the resize
  label (the templatized peer of the web inline `Resize column ${columnKey}`), the spoken width value (the
  peer of `aria-valuenow`, with a unit Apple's adjustable element should announce), and the gesture hint
  (the WAI-ARIA window-splitter semantics VoiceOver does not narrate natively). The `{{column}}` /
  `{{width}}` interpolation tokens are resolved by DataTableResizerProjector.interpolate.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept
  in a per-surface table ("DataTableResizer") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings. In test
  / preview bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the value below, keeping the labels deterministic.
*/

/* --- Native VoiceOver additions (no web `t()` key exists; the source is anonymous) --- */

/* The accessible label; {{column}} is the column key (templatized peer of web `Resize column ${columnKey}`). */
"table.resizer.label" = "Resize column {{column}}";

/* The spoken width value; {{width}} is the current whole-point width (peer of web `aria-valuenow`). */
"table.resizer.value" = "{{width}} points";

/* The VoiceOver hint describing how to resize (the window-splitter semantics VoiceOver does not narrate). */
"table.resizer.hint" = "Drag, or use the arrow keys, to resize the column";
